    "reason": "The Japanese word '策略' (sakuryaku) primarily refers to a scheme, stratagem, ruse, or artifice. While 'trick' can have this meaning, the English lemma 'trick' (noun) is highly polysemous and also commonly refers to magic tricks (e.g., 手品, マジック), practical jokes (e.g., いたずら), or a knack/skill (e.g., コツ). '策略' does not cover these other common meanings, making it a narrow translation for the general concept of 'trick' in daily life. It is also a more formal word than what a general learner might expect for the broad concept of 'trick'. Further clarification on the intended core sense of 'trick' is needed.",
